<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap-text wrap-text--intro center">
    <p class="eyebrow">Join the lab</p>
    <h1>Come and work with us</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      We are building one of the best evolutionary ecology labs in the world. That
      is the ambition, and it is the standard we hire to.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section--tight">
  <div class="wrap-text">
    <h2>What the lab is like</h2>
    <p>
      Our aim is science that sits right at the top of the field, which means
      choosing big questions over safe ones. Thinking big is difficult. It comes
      from reading widely, knowing the classics well enough to see the great
      unanswered questions, and then having the confidence to go after them. Aim
      high; I will always back you.
    </p>
    <p>
      A few things follow from that, and they are worth knowing before you write
      to me. Everyone reads, and reads outside their own corner of the field.
      Everyone writes, and everyone publishes: research that is not published did
      not happen, so the rule is write first, write often, because editing is
      easier than drafting. Everyone attends the Lizard Island field seasons in
      May and June and in October and November, regardless of their own PhD topic,
      and at least one dissertation chapter comes from Lizard Island data. That
      ties every one of us into the long-term study and guarantees you leave having
      contributed to it.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are also expected to rest. Field seasons are intense and the hours are
      long, but that is not a description of the whole year. I would far rather you
      were rested and switched on than running on empty, and I trust you to manage
      your own time, take holidays, and travel without consulting me.
    </p>
    <p>
      The full picture, including my mentoring commitments to you, is in the
      <a href="/files/Stroud_Lab_Handbook.pdf">lab handbook</a>. It is worth reading
      before you apply.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cards">

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">PhD students</p>
        <h3>Graduate students</h3>
        <p>
          Students join through the School of Biological Sciences at Georgia Tech,
          through Biology, Quantitative Biosciences (QBioS), or Bioinformatics.
          Applications are handled by the graduate programme, but write to me
          before you apply.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tell me what you find interesting and why, and what you want to work on.
          A short, specific email beats a long, generic one. Attach a CV.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">Postdocs</p>
        <h3>Postdoctoral researchers</h3>
        <p>
          I am always glad to hear from prospective postdocs, particularly people
          interested in developing their own line of work within the lab's themes.
          Get in touch early if you are thinking about a fellowship, since the good
          ones close a long way in advance and the proposal is better when we write
          it together.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">Undergraduates</p>
        <h3>Georgia Tech undergraduates</h3>
        <p>
          We take undergraduate researchers every semester, and several have gone
          on to publish and to present at international meetings. Some run senior
          research theses; some come to Miami for the field seasons. If you are a
          Georgia Tech student and this interests you, email me.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap-text">
    <h2>Everyone is welcome here</h2>
    <p>
      Everyone in this lab deserves patience, generosity, and basic kindness.
      Harassment, discrimination, or condescension toward anyone, including
      labmates, collaborators, and the staff and field crews who make our work
      possible, has no place here and will not be tolerated. A team only works
      when people feel safe and valued in it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everyone also has a voice, and using it early is expected rather than
      merely permitted. If something is wrong, or could be better, I want to hear
      it before it becomes something larger.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <a class="btn btn--accent" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email James</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
